From b9829f5607a65922d435a4fc781f3ebe4ff4680f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Phase1 Draft (Claude, for Terhi review)" <draft@local>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 14:37:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] refactor(likelihood): unify the two spatial-integral
 branches into spatial_refinement_integral (eq. 24) -- exp(f_xy[c] (+ b_0[m]))
 contracted against refinement-cell areas; the no-covariate grid is the same
 atom with uniform areas 1/n_xy^2. Constructor now derives
 integration_field_indices / integration_cov_indices / integration_areas as
 plain NumPy arrays once (from int_df in the covariate case), so NO
 pandas/GeoPandas object is read inside traced likelihood code (int_df itself
 stays in args for plotting). Rewires both model fns; rate_xy deterministics
 kept as trace sites (now noqa'd in both fns -- the atom recomputes exp(f_xy)
 on the indexed subset). DECLARED EXPRESSION CHANGE (not a pure lift): the
 plain branch becomes exp(f_xy[cells]) @ areas instead of
 sum(exp(f_xy)[cells])/n_xy^2 -- algebraically equal, different rounding
 sequence; acceptance criterion was rtol=2e-6 on all value+gradient pins;
 OBSERVED: pins bit-identical anyway (worst relative movement 0.0), so no
 re-baselining was ultimately needed. Atom unit tests: independent float64
 reference, plain special case, refinement invariance (I9) at atom level,
 finite gradients w.r.t. (f_xy, b_0). 31/31.

